course: dictionary
lesson: 14381
title: Orient: finding your way and facing the right direction
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Orient is a word about direction. To orient yourself means to find out where you are and which way you are facing. «When we reached the forest, we used a map to orient ourselves.» The clue is the map: it helps you work out where you are.
explain: Orient can also mean to turn or place something so it faces a certain way. «She oriented the map so that north pointed to the top of the page.» Try swapping in "turned" or "set": "She turned the map so that north pointed to the top..." still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: The word can also mean to aim something at a group or purpose. «The new science course is oriented to beginners.» This means the course is designed for beginners. Orient is a verb, so look for its forms: orient, orients, oriented, orienting.
fact: Orient means to find out where you are, or to turn something to face a direction.
fact: Orienteering is a sport where you use a map and a compass to find your way across country.
fact: «Oriented north» means turned so that it faces north.
fact: The old-fashioned noun «the Orient» meant the countries of East Asia; today we usually say East Asia or Asia.
fact: A new pupil who gets oriented at school learns where things are and how the day works.
exercise: «We used a compass to orient the map before we set off.» What does orient mean here? | *Turn the map to face the right direction | Tear the map into small pieces | Colour in the map's roads | Fold the map away in a bag
exercise: «The new pupil took a week to get oriented at school.» What does getting oriented mean? | Losing the way home | Painting the classroom walls | Leaving school early for the day | *Finding out where things are and how the school day works
exercise: «The new science course is oriented to beginners.» What does this mean? | *The course is designed for beginners | The course is only for teachers | The course is cancelled for everyone | The course is full of lost students
test: «Before the hike, Sam used a compass to orient himself.» What does orient himself mean? | *Work out where he was and which way he faced | Pack his lunch and go home | Read a book about birds | Lose his way on purpose
test: Which sentence uses orient to mean turning something to face a direction? | «The bus was late this morning.» | «They ate their lunch by the lake.» | «She sang a song at the concert.» | *«He oriented the shape so its flat side faced down.»
exam: Which word means to find out where you are or which way you are facing? | Compass | *Orient | Orienteering | Oriented | Oriental
